# `optim::Lsr1Result`

What `l_sr1_trust_region` returns: the flat solution, the objective, the gradient norm and the exit flag.

`params` is the solution as one flat vector (the block form also returns the blocks in their own shapes). `objective_value` and `objective` give the final objective, `gradient_norm` the 2-norm of its gradient, and `step_norm` the last step. `iteration` and `function_evaluations` count the work (a trust-region step may be tried more than once). `converged`, `exit_flag` and `message` say how it ended, and `state` holds the method's memory.

## Fields

### `params`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

The flat solution vector.

### `state`

`optim::Lsr1State`, default `{}`.

The method's memory.

### `objective`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

The final objective.

### `iteration`

`std::int64_t`, default `0`.

Iterations.

### `function_evaluations`

`std::int64_t`, default `0`.

Objective evaluations.

### `objective_value`

`double`, default `+inf`.

The final objective as a number.

### `gradient_norm`

`double`, default `+inf`.

The 2-norm of the final gradient.

### `step_norm`

`double`, default `0`.

The last step.

### `converged`

`bool`, default `false`.

Whether the gradient test was met.

### `exit_flag`

`optim::Lsr1ExitFlag`, default `MaxIterations`.

Why it stopped.

### `message`

`std::string`, default `empty`.

A sentence about the ending.

## Guidance

Check `converged` before using `params`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Every field of a result for a quadratic.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto objective = [](const Series &x) { return (x - 3.0).square().sum(); };

  const optim::Lsr1Result result = optim::l_sr1_trust_region(objective, pluss::series::make({0.0, 0.0}));
  out.writeln("converged =", result.converged, ", exit =", optim::lsr1_exit_flag_name(result.exit_flag), ", message =", result.message);
  out.writeln("params =", result.params.items<double>(), ", objective =", result.objective_value);
  out.writeln("gradient norm =", result.gradient_norm, ", step norm =", result.step_norm);
  out.writeln("iterations =", result.iteration, ", evaluations =", result.function_evaluations);
}
```

### Example 2

A run that does not finish.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto rosenbrock = [](const Series &x) {
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    return (1.0 - a).square() + 100.0 * (b - a.square()).square();
  };

  optim::Lsr1SolveOptions options;
  options.max_iterations = 3;
  const optim::Lsr1Result result = optim::l_sr1_trust_region(rosenbrock, pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0}), options);
  out.writeln("converged =", result.converged, ", exit =", optim::lsr1_exit_flag_name(result.exit_flag), ", gradient norm =", result.gradient_norm);
}
```

### Example 3

Evaluations versus iterations. Rejected trust-region steps cost evaluations without counting as iterations.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const auto rosenbrock = [](const Series &x) {
    const Series a = x.select(0, 0), b = x.select(0, 1);
    return (1.0 - a).square() + 100.0 * (b - a.square()).square();
  };

  const optim::Lsr1Result result = optim::l_sr1_trust_region(rosenbrock, pluss::series::make({-1.2, 1.0}));
  out.writeln("iterations =", result.iteration, ", evaluations =", result.function_evaluations);
}
```

